UID:10016928-1776430800-1776439800@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Intro to WNC Invasive Plant ID
DESCRIPTION:Intro to WNC Invasive Plant ID\nwith Erin Canter \nFriday\, April 17  |  1 – 3:30pm \nBRN – Elective |  BREG – Elective \nREGISTER HERE \nIn this beginners’ course\, participants will learn strategies for plant ID and use them to identify plants that are invasive to Western North Carolina. We’ll discuss the impact of invasive plants and other invasive species\, and introduce strategies for their management and control in our own properties and public spaces. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nErin Canter is a Southern Appalachian Naturalist who specializes in southeastern ecology. She worked as the Manager of Science Literacy and Research at a nonprofit education center in the Great Smoky Mountains\, working with all ages to explore their bioregion through science and hands-on exploration\, before moving to this side of the mountains in early 2024. She now works at American Conservation Experience here in WNC\, helping young people begin their conservation careers through applied conservation projects in the region. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\n\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/intro-to-wnc-invasive-plant-id/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Adult-Ed-Course-Jpgs-13.jpg
END:VEVENT
