X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/ecology-of-the-native-azalea-collection-walk/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T103000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230456
CREATED:20260324T144748Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260324T144748Z
UID:10017009-1776502800-1776508200@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Ecology of the Native Azalea Collection Walk
DESCRIPTION:Ecology of the Native Azalea Collection Walk\nwith Lauren Lampley \nSaturday\, April 18 | 9 – 10:30 am \nBRN – Elective \nREGISTER HERE \nFor Native Azalea Day\, join Adult Education Coordinator\, Lauren Lampley\, on an ecology walk through the Native Azalea Collection highlighting different plants\, wildlife\, and ecosystems found within the collection. We will also discuss how the different wetlands and creeks play into the ecology of the space and how our Community Science Projects make use of the unique space for science. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nLauren Lampley began her career at Grandfather Mountain Stewardship Foundation as a Park Naturalist which solidified Lauren’s interests in ecology and a passion for teaching others. She has led walks and hikes in a variety of subjects from Geology to Birding and especially enjoys learning and teaching about our local ecology. She currently works at the NC Arboretum as the Adult Education Coordinator managing all the programming hosted through the Adult Education Department. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/ecology-of-the-native-azalea-collection-walk/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/OppenheimPhoto-NCArboretum-Spring-2016-0028.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-yoga/2026-04-18/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T110000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230443
CREATED:20251229T160442Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251230T151634Z
UID:10005957-1776504600-1776510000@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:The Art of Yoga
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Museum for a harmonious blend of artistic inspiration and mindful movement! Our Saturday sessions are from 9:30–11am on January 24\, February 21\, March 28\, April 18\, May 23\, and June 20.  Experience how close looking at art and practicing yoga in the beautiful spaces of the Museum can foster relaxation and connection. \nEach class pass and yoga session includes a guided mindful looking session in one of the Museum’s current exhibitions. After class\, you’re invited to the John & Robyn Horn Education Center (level 3) for a complimentary cup of tea and artful conversation. \nAll levels are welcome. Please bring your own yoga mat. No mat\, no problem\, the Museum has some extra mats to lend. Loose-fitting clothing is recommended\, ensuring ease of movement as you flow through your practice. \n\nBenefits: \n\nMindful Connection: connect with the present moment as you flow through your practice in relation to a thought-provoking artwork.\nArtistic Inspiration: take advantage of practicing yoga in one of the most inspiring interior spaces in Asheville. Fuel your creativity and enhance the mind-body connection while meeting other artful yogis.\n\nPractical Tips: \n\nArrive a little early to settle into the Museum’s ambiance and find your preferred spot in the gallery.\nSpace is limited; advance registration is required.\n\nThe Art of Yoga series is taught by certified yoga instructors and Museum staff. For more information\, email learn@ashevilleart.org or call 828.253.3227 x121. \n\n\nRegister Now
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-yoga/2026-04-18/
LOCATION:NC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/DSC_1624-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
