DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T120000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230456
CREATED:20260408T153754Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T153754Z
UID:10017154-1776506400-1776513600@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Guided Trail Walk
DESCRIPTION:Hit the trails and learn more about The North Carolina Arboretum’s botanically diverse forest with a guided trail walk! April through October\, this free hiking program is led by trained volunteer guides who take small groups of participants along woodland trails and through a variety of forest types. Depending on the season and each guide’s area of expertise\, topics of discussion may include wildflowers\, plant and tree identification\, natural history and more. \nGuided trail walks are limited to 15 people\, including the guide\, and are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age. Groups depart from the Baker Visitor Center Lobby on Tuesdays at 1 p.m. and Saturdays at 10 a.m. and 1 p.m.. \nWalks last 1.5 – 2.5 hours\, are approximately one to two miles in length. As this program is held rain or shine\, all participants should dress appropriately for the weather. \nThere is no pre-registration; walks are first-come first served and sign up sheets are located in the Baker Visitors Center. \nWalks are FREE; however\, donations to The North Carolina Arboretum Society are appreciated. Regular parking fees apply. Arboretum Society Members always park free. \nKnow Before You Go\n\nGuided Trail Walks are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age.\nGuided Trail Walks are rain or shine and all participants should be dressed comfortably and for the weather.\nHikes cover 1-2 miles and last 1.5-2 hours.\nWell-behaved leashed pets are welcome to accompany their owners. In the rare case that a pet is disruptive or negatively impacts the experience\, the pet and its owner may be asked to excuse themselves from the guided walk.
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-6/2026-04-18/
CATEGORIES:Guided Trail Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Birders-on-Cove-Hardwood-Trail-GSMNP-TN-Apr-16-1-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/native-azalea-day-4/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T150000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230456
CREATED:20260204T182701Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T162025Z
UID:10016901-1776506400-1776524400@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Native Azalea Day
DESCRIPTION:Native Azalea Day\nApril 18\, 2026\n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m.\nVisit the gardens this spring for Native Azalea Day\, an invitation to celebrate and experience azaleas through the eyes of plant enthusiasts\, botanists\, and artists. For one day only\, visitors can observe as plein air artists capture the scene in paint and pen\, learn about the garden and its collection on a walking tour\, and participate in hands-on activities for children and adults. \nA shuttle to the Collection will be available between 10:00 a.m. and 3:00 p.m.\, departing to and from the Baker Visitor Center throughout the event. Visitors are also welcome to walk to the Native Azalea Collection from the Gatehouse Parking Lot using Old Mill Road to Bent Creek Road\, or can park at the Baker Visitor Center and walk down Running Cedar Road to Bent Creek Road. Walkers should be prepared to travel one mile over unpaved roads and paths. \nSpecial thanks to Community Partner Carolina Native Nursery for sponsoring Native Azalea Day. \nEvent Schedule\n8:30 – 9:30 a.m: Pre-registered “Ecology of the Native Azalea Collection” with Lauren Lampley \n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m: Tabling with local environmental organizations including Carolina Native Nursery\, NC Native Plant Society\, Azalea Society of America\, Arboretum Adult Education Citizen Science\, Dayna of Solstice Handmade\, and Graham County  \n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m: Ecology scavenger hunt with Hemlock Restoration Initiative \n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m: Dissecting scope and interactive drawing activities with Educator\, Erin Ellis. \n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m: Cyanotyping activity  \n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m: Music with SARAH \n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m: Food and drink provided by The Arbor Eatery \n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m: Plein Art Painting Group of Asheville  \n10:30 – 11:15 a.m: Pre-registered walking tour with curator\, Carson Ellis \n11:30 a.m. – 12:00 p.m: Pre-registered walking tour with volunteer docent \n12:30 – 1:00 p.m: Pre-registered walking tour with Lauren Best\, Native Azalea Conservation Assistant \n1:30 – 2:00 p.m: Pre-registered walking tour with volunteer docent \n3:00 p.m: Last shuttle departs Azalea Collection \nAll activities\, unless otherwise noted\, are included with general admission fees. \nThis event is part of Spring Into the Arb! Celebrate the return of spring with a series of events and happenings throughout March\, April\, May and June! Spring is a time of renewal and emergence\, and The North Carolina Arboretum is excited to welcome this season with plant shows\, nature programs\, education\, music\, art and more!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/native-azalea-day-4/
LOCATION:Native Azalea Collection
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/20230429_cantrell_azaleaday_123-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
