SUMMARY:Cat Gap John Rock
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n[https://maps.app.goo.gl/wh85xMeRV
 tcg3QKD](https://maps.app.goo.gl/wh85xMeRVtcg3QKD)\n\njoin me for a smalle
 r group\, non-intensive out and back to the John Rock overlook\, taking ti
 me to appreciate the emerging flora and spring blooms.\n\napprox 4.7 miles
  and 875 feet of elevation gain\n\nwell behaved dogs welcome\, but they wi
 ll need to be leashed for their safety as we approach the rock face\n\nsay
  2 - 2.5 mph pace\n\ncarpooling is encouraged due to limited parking at th
 e trailhead as the site is under construction\n\ngear up as appropriate\, 
 trekking poles are an option. bring a snack as we'll take a break mid-hike
 . and plenty of water\n\nground rules:\n\n1) if you sign up\, show up or c
 hange your status. a no-show may undercut a motivated wait-lister. (repeat
 ed no-shows will have consequences) likewise\, if you're on the wait list 
 at the time of the hike\, don't presume to just show up\n\n2 ) be sure you
  are in adequate physical shape to complete the event\n\n3) show considera
 tion by emphasizing group effort and group cohesion. I hike for stress red
 uction and want to keep it that way. i reserve the right to remove anyone 
 from an event if words or actions indicate the need to do so\n\nLEGALESE\n
 This Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transpo
 rtation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for thei
 r own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical c
 onditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to onesel
 f and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can
  assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up for this event\
 , participant understands and agrees
