BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/rising-stars-concert-with-andrew-ning/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T193000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230443
CREATED:20260216T135717Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260323T210530Z
UID:10006518-1776794400-1776799800@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Rising Stars Concert with Andrew Ning
DESCRIPTION:Rising Stars Concert is a collaboration between the Asheville Chamber Music Series and the Asheville Art Museum\, featuring North Carolina musicians embarking on a major concert career. The event is sponsored and made possible by Heidi DuBose. \nPianist: Andrew Ning \nPurchase Tickets\nRepertoire:\n\nSergei Prokofiev\, Suggestion Diabolique\, Op. 4\, No. 4\nFrédéric Chopin\, Ballade No. 3 in A-flat major\, Op. 47\nGeorge Gershwin\, Three Preludes (No. 1 Allegro ben ritmato e deciso; No. 2 Andante con moto;\nNo. 3 Agitato)\nJohann Sebastian Bach\, Prelude and Fugue in D major\, BWV 850\nJoseph Haydn\, Piano Sonata in C major\, Hob. XVI:50: I. Allegro\nLudwig van Beethoven\, Piano Sonata No. 30 in E major\, Op. 109 (I. Vivace\, ma non troppo;\nII. Prestissimo)\nJohannes Brahms\, Intermezzo in A minor (Op. 118 No. 1); Intermezzo in A major (Op. 118 No. 2)\nFrédéric Chopin\, Ballade No. 4 in F minor\, Op. 5\n\nAbout the Rising Star:\nAndrew Ning is a senior at Riverside High School in Greer\, South Carolina. Guided by his teacher\, Lisa Kiser\, he enjoys participating in piano competitions at regional\, state\, and national levels. Some of his recent achievements include first place in the 2025 Asheville Area Piano Forum Piano Competition (Advanced level)\, first prize in the 2025 W. Darr Wise Piano Competition (Division 1)\, and first in the 2024 SC-MTNA Piano Duet competition (senior level). Andrew was the principal keyboardist/pianist of the Young Artist Orchestra (YAO)\, Greenville\, South Carolina. He recently won the YAO Concerto Competition and performed the third movement of Grieg’s piano concerto at the Peace Center. Andrew is the manager and organizer for a musical recital program for a local nursing home. Beyond the realm of music\, he swims competitively and is captain of his high school State team. \nThe Steinway piano is available to the Asheville Art Museum through the courtesy of the Asheville Chamber Music Series.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/rising-stars-concert-with-andrew-ning/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Performance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/image0-scaled.jpeg
END:VEVENT
