LAST-MODIFIED:20260215T203043Z
UID:10035674-1776855600-1776866400@www.riverartsdistrict.com
SUMMARY:Gel Plate Monoprinting – Wabi-Sabi Approach
DESCRIPTION:Get your hands inky and explore the beauty of imperfection with spontaneous mark making\, textured layers\, motifs and playful experimentation – rooted in the Wabi Sabi approach to Mono Printing\, celebrating the beauty of the unrepeatable. \nClasses explore a variety of techniques and materials for creating monoprints. Students will learn to use a gel plate\, brayer\, stencils\, rice paper\, textures\, paints\, and more. \nYou will have use of 1 5″x7″ Gelli mono printing plate\, inking plate\, brayer\, acrylic and ink\, a variety of papers to print on\, mylar stencils. and rubber stamps. \nStudents bring gloves if desired\, beverage and lunch.
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/wabi-sabi-monoprint-workshop/2026-04-22/
LOCATION:Trackside Studios\, 375 Depot Street\, Asheville\, 28801
CATEGORIES:Classes
