X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Mountains To Sea Trail Hiking Club": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiking-club/events/314103936/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_mountains_to_sea_trail_hiking_club
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_314103936@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260418T030446Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T110000
SUMMARY:Fresh Market toward visitor's Center
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nWe will meet
  near the Fresh Market on Highway 25 and walk 2.5 miles in on the MTS trai
 l and then back to the Fresh Market. This trail comes out on the road at l
 east twice\, so keep this in mind with dogs on the trail.\n\nThis is a fai
 rlly easy hike\, and we go at a high average to low advanced speed\, which
  is roughly about 3.0 to 3.2 mph. There are no super long hills. It's pret
 ty undulating all the way. The biggest hill is at the beginning.\n\nWell b
 ehaved dogs on leashes are welcome to attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park cl
 osest to the forest on the side where Haywood Appliance is.\n\nMountains-t
 o-Sea-Trail hikes are designed for fitness and community among people who 
 are already reasonably fit. It's not an endurance hike by any means\, but 
 it is designed so we can get our hearts beating a bit while still being ab
 le to have a conversation and meet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll ci
 rcle up and introduce ourselves briefly. There will be a person who is a s
 weep. This person is the person who walks last and makes sure no one gets 
 lost.\n\nWe leave the parking spot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature brea
 k\, we wait fo you\, but it's not a hike where we stop and take photos or 
 frequent breaks. We basically keep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then tu
 rn around after a short (approximately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that 
 same pace on the way back. If we get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are nor
 mally finished around 10:50.\n\nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning tha
 t we hike in and turn around half way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/314103936/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260403T105758Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260403T105758Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/walking-meditation-qigong-9/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T100000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230456
CREATED:20260309T172333Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260311T194930Z
UID:10016992-1777021200-1777024800@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Walking Meditation & Qigong
DESCRIPTION:Walking Meditation & Qigong\nwith Jenne Sluder \nFriday\, April 24  |  9 – 10am \nREGISTER HERE \nEnjoy a slow\, mindful walking meditation through the gardens\, practicing breath awareness and sensory attention to touch the deep peace and simple wonders of quiet time in nature. This session begins with a series of gentle and easy Qigong movements to clear the mind\, release tension\, support the body and brain’s natural healing processes\, and generate a sense of inner calm. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nJenne Sluder\, MA C-IAYT holds a Master’s in Transpersonal Psychology: Ecopsychology from Naropa University. She is a certified yoga therapist\, mind-body specialist\, and meditation instructor. Jenne is also an environmental educator and spent her undergrad years working and studying under the direct mentorship of Thomas Berry and Joseph Cornell at the Center for Education\, Imagination\, and the Natural World\, continuing her studies in nature-based rites of passage with the School of Lost Borders and the Earth-Based Institute. An Asheville native\, Jenne works one-on-one with individuals and with groups using mindfulness-based\, nature-based\, and compassion-centric mind-body therapies towards personal and collective well-being. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/walking-meditation-qigong-9/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Jenne-Sluder-Yoga-1-1536x1097-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/geology-of-the-blue-ridge-field-class-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T163000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230456
CREATED:20260309T181123Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260415T153039Z
UID:10016994-1777030200-1777048200@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Geology of the Blue Ridge Field Class
DESCRIPTION:Geology of the Blue Ridge Field Class\nwith Anton DuMars \nFriday\, April 24 | Meet in Brevard at 12\, class time is 12 – 4 pm \nBRN – Core \nREGISTER HERE \nOn this Field Experience\, we will observe and interpret evidence of Appalachian mountain-building events. Participants can put their hands on a 380+/- million-year-old pluton and observe their post-uplift weathering\, jointing\, and exfoliation. In addition\, participants observe and interpret river processes\, transport\, and depositional environments of sediments derived from up-gradient sources. The experience includes on-site geologic map reading and interpretation. \nThis off-site program has stops in the Pisgah Forest near Brevard NC along The Pisgah Highway including Daniel Ridge and the Davidson River. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy to moderate trails. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nAnton DuMars\, a resident of Black Mountain\, NC\, is an adjunct professor at the College of Charleston. His geological interests include fluvial\, deltaic\, and coastal processes. Ideally\, he’s spending time on a hiking trail or aboard his sailboat. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\n\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/geology-of-the-blue-ridge-field-class-2/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Rock-Overhang-at-Moore-Cove-Falls-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
