SUMMARY:AMC Sunday Ecstatic Dance CCLD Fundraiser @WWC w/DJ Bobcat
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Movement Collective\nSunday\, April 26th\n\nCCLD Fun
 draiser at Warren Wilson College\nw/ DJ Bobcat \\(Bob Swoap\\) \\| Support
  Kris Hostikka\nAbout DJ Bobcat\n\nBob crafts journeys that invite dancers
  to deeply connect: with themselves\, others\, nature\, and the music. He 
 layers genres and world rhythms into an emotionally engaging set. At Warre
 n Wilson College -- where he is professor of psychology and expressive art
 s therapy -- Bob facilitates ecstatic dance as a part of the community wel
 lness program\, bringing a grounded\, experienced presence to the floor. F
 avorite place to dance: outside at the WWC Pavilion. IG: @bob.swoap\n\n\\~
 \\~\\~\n\n\\*\\* Please note that the dance starts at Warm up. The doors c
 lose promptly at Opening Circle and people who arrive late will be turned 
 away. Please be on time to ensure a safe and secure container. \\*\\*\n\nT
 icket Price: $15-30 or name your price.\nNo one turned away for lack of fu
 nds!\n\n\\~\\~\\~\n\nPre-registration Recommended:\nhttps://ashevillemovem
 entcollective.org/event/\n\nVOLUNTEER!\nWe need volunteers. Volunteer and 
 dance for free! Register to volunteer at: [https://ashevillemovementcollec
 tive.org/volunteer/](https://ashevillemovementcollective.org/volunteer/?fb
 clid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAYnJpZBExVTF6aExURExqbndxM3JFUHNydGMGYXBwX2lkEDIyMjA
 zOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR6puHJaet_dJGFESCItA4rMD5vM_RHt9QzUSALulddRTAtGKexRuWuiB
 E8tDw_aem_vXP_JSWUu1NrAFuKa--PQA)\n\nIMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENTS:\nDoor will c
 lose at the beginning of the opening circle. Please note: NO ENTRY AFTER O
 PENING CIRCLE BOTH WAVES!\n\nCollective agreements:\n[https://ashevillemov
 ementcollective.org/our-dance/](https://ashevillemovementcollective.org/ou
 r-dance/?fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAYnJpZBExVTF6aExURExqbndxM3JFUHNydGMGYXBw
 X2lkEDIyMjAzOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR5CSyB7238bGlkEsU_Cg_jsh0446YHLe69W1y3KV5-T6o
 MaN-7Z3q32wDznUA_aem_wUhim1G2JnrnWxIQYKCcIA)\n\nAbout AMC:\nAsheville Move
 ment Collective envisions a world that moves in harmony where all are free
  to be their authentic selves within a loving community. Our mission and a
