SUMMARY:April 26th Community Cuddles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space.[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-U
 S/ticketing/april-26th-community-cuddles)**[Click HERE to register!](https
 ://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/april-26th-community-cuddles)**\n\n**This
  is a non-sexual touch based event that invites participants to explore pl
 atonic intimacy in a safe environment** with like-minded people. We respec
 t personal boundaries and through a supportive framework of mutual agreeme
 nts that maximize safety and create a space of easy openness and compassio
 nate connection.\nAt this event we have the chance to normalize touch with
  clear boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, consent-based touch. 
 We allow ourselves to be seen. We have fun.\nWe welcome people of all back
 grounds\, genders\, ethnicities\, relationship styles\, sexualities\, size
 s\, and ages (18+).\n\n**THE RULES**\n1\\. Clothes stay on for the whole e
 vent\\.\n2\\. You do not have to touch anyone at this event\\.\n3\\. You m
 ust receive a verbal YES before you touch anyone\\.\n4\\. Take care of you
 rself and those you choose to interact with\\.\n5\\. Speak up if you have 
 a question\\\, concern\\\, or if you need assistance with anything during 
 the event\\.\n6\\. All emotions are welcome\\- we love vulnerability\\.\n*
 *WHY CUDDLE?**\nTouch is a basic human need\, and many of us do not get en
 ough\; most people don’t even know they are missing touch\, or have a wa
 y to ask for touch without sexualizing it. We believe deeply in the power 
 of touch\, and the importance of communication and consent in creating a s
 afe space for touch.\nCUDDLING WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers sou
 nds weird or scary to most people. “Will I like it?” “What if someon
 e wants to touch me and I don’t want to?” “What if I say yes and it
 ’s not what I want?” “What if I really want to touch someone and the
 y say no?” These are all normal questions. The answer is that this is a 
 space created to ask for exactly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you d
 on’t want. Many people start out nervous at a cuddle event & most are re
 ally glad they came.\n\n**Schedule:**\n6:50-7pm: Arrive with snacks to sha
 re! Get comfortable\, meet\, mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circle- it
 s mandatory. We will set our container\, talk about personal boundaries\, 
 communication\, & consent.\n7:15pm: Icebreakers and connective activities.
 \n8:00pm: Open cuddling! You MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ before to
 uching or cuddling with anybody at this event. If you are not sure how to 
 do this – great! – we will talk about it during the welcome circle.\n1
 0:50pm: Closing Circle\, cleanup and head home.\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n* ARRIVE
  ON TIME: It is important that all participants arrive before the Welcome 
 Circle. The Welcome Circle serves the purpose of creating the safe space f
 or consensual\, non-sexual touch between participants and making sure that
  everyone is informed about consent.\n* Please arrive clean & as scent fre
 e as possible.\n* BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this
  event.\n\n**WHAT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to share\, 
 a friend\, a date – whatever cuddle accessories you like! The only thing
  that you are required to bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nThese events 
 are not "gender balanced".\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriou
 sly!** If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is n
 ot safe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to 
 doing our best to create a safe environment which means that if someone is
  causing harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this i
 ncludes harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind surv
 ivors and know that some of our participants are here to heal from touch b
 ased trauma.\n\n\\*refund policy-\nFull refund if you cancel 7 days before
  the event or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure t
 o covid/flu.\nCredit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days
  before an event.\nNo refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or n
 o-show.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-cuddle-collective/events/31
 3769609/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260313T172006Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260313T172006Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
