SUMMARY:May 2nd An Evening of Spicy/Sensual Snuggles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space.[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-U
 S/ticketing/may-2nd-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles)**[CLICK HERE TO PURCHA
 SE YOU TICKET AND RESERVE YOUR SPACE FOR THIS EVENT.](https://www.zeffy.co
 m/en-US/ticketing/may-2nd-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles)**[ ](https://www
 .zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/may-2nd-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles)\n\n**Wh
 at is a Sensual Snuggle Event?**\nThis is a sweet & welcoming event where 
 we practice and use verbal consent to connect and share touch. We talk abo
 ut boundaries and practice both saying and receiving a “no”. In this s
 pace it is common to see people cuddle\, share massage\, have their hair b
 rushed\, kiss\, expose nipples\, play\, laugh\, cry\, and be vulnerable. T
 his is a sober space where we can relax and connect with other humans who 
 are seeking touch based connection.\nWe strive for this to be a safe event
 . Safe touch enhances our ability to connect with and trust people. When w
 e are in a space of safety\, we are able to relax\, feel comfort\, and be 
 vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\n1- We ask for what we want an wait for
  a yes before touching others.\n2- We say no if we don’t want to do some
 thing.\n3- We try to receive a no with grace and not take it personally.\n
 4- We arrive on time\, clean (as scent free as possible)\, and sober.\n5- 
 We keep our pants/shorts on at this event. (Tops are optional\; this is a 
 sensual space\, not a sexual space.)\n6- We are here to connect with other
 s. Connection can be verbal\, platonic\, or spicy!\n7- We welcome diversit
 y. Isms and Phobias are not welcome here!\n\n**Who should attend:**\nPeopl
 e who are interested in safely exploring touch and sensuality with strange
 rs. This includes people who are single\, people who are not single\, coup
 les\, folks who are new to town and looking for connection\, people of all
 /any genders and sexual orientations\, people of all ages (18 and up). Peo
 ple who understand and respect consent\, who will take care of themselves 
 and people around them. This event is queer-normative. The guest list will
  include all genders\, orientations\, ages\, and personalities. If that’
 s not your thing… This is not the event for you.\n***Who should NOT atte
 nd:***\n-People who are only looking for a sex party.\n-People who do not 
 understand and respect consent.\n-People who have extreme fear of setting 
 and speaking their personal boundaries\; in order to create a safe space w
 e need to know that you will say “no” if you feel a no.\n-People who a
 re homophobic\, racist\, sexist\, ageist\, ableist…\n-People under 18 ye
 ars of age.\n***Schedule of the Evening***\n\n* 6:50pm Doors Open\, Mix & 
 Mingle\n* 7:00pm We gather in a circle to meet each other\, build a contai
 ner\, cover consent and boundary setting and discuss event agreements. The
 n we will play a few intimacy building games to meet and connect with othe
 r people in the room. Please make sure you arrive on-time!\n* 8:15pm Once 
 the container is built we will have self directed snuggling and sensual in
 teractions until the end of the party.\n* 10:50pm Closing Circle\; a time 
 to re-center and connect as a group to verbally share anything that came u
 p at the event or to voice gratitude to someone(s) you enjoyed interacting
  with.\n* 11:00pm cleanup & head home\; you are welcome to help.\n\n**We t
 ake individual and group safety seriously!** If you experience\, see\, or 
 know that one of our participants is not safe to be at this event we want 
 to know about it. We are committed to doing our best to create a safe envi
 ronment which means that if someone is causing harm (physical or mental) t
 hat person is not welcome here (this includes harm that takes place outsid
 e of our events). We stand behind survivors and know that some of our part
 icipants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\nThese events are not
  "gender balanced"[. Check out our website for more information about this
  decision. ](http://holdmeavl.com/why-i-dont-gender-balance-events/)\n\n**
 Simple definitions/clarifications-** Platonic- marked by the absence of ro
 mance or sex.\nMost of the interactions we have with friends and strangers
  are platonic.\nSensual- gratification of the senses or the indulgence of 
 appetite.\nWe might feel sensual when we feel someone's breath on our neck
  or experience a extra long and slow caress.\nSexual- having or involving 
 sex.\nOften involving one more more peoples genitals\; perhaps seeking org
 asm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full refund if you cancel 7 days before the event 
 or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid. Cr
 edit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before an event
 . No refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-cuddle-collective/events/31
 4309275/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260416T044010Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260416T044010Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
