X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Runners": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/312835128/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_runners
X-SOURCE:Asheville Runners
UID:event_312835128@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260418T030447Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T200000
SUMMARY:Thursday Run 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Runners\nCome run 1\, 3\, or 6 miles and stay for a 
 beer and soccer tennis after at Olde London Road.\n\nRoutes-\n1 miler:\nRI
 GHT out of OLR parking lot\nContinue around roundabout at Clingman\, and h
 ead toward the river on Lyman St.\nRIGHT on River Arts Place\nCross Rivers
 ide onto the Greenway\nRight on the Greenway to the Craven St Park put in 
 (the dock)\nTurn around and go back the same way to OLR\n\n3 miler:\nStart
  the same as 1 miler\nContinue onto Craven St. Bridge\nLEFT onto Greenway 
 after bridge\nFollow Greenway all the way until it ends at Haywood Rd.\nRI
 GHT onto Haywood Rd\, go across the bridge\nCross the Roundabout at Robert
 s St. and continue onto Clingman\nContinue on Clingman\nLEFT onto Owens Be
 ll Lane\nLEFT onto Hilliard at the top of the hill\nLEFT onto W Haywood\, 
 follow all the way down to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts\nFollow Roberts back
  to OLR\nPass OLR to Bartlett\, turn around and come back to OLR\n\n6 mile
 r:\nAfter the W Haywood downhill to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts St. take to
  Lyman and head back to the Greenway\nLEFT onto the Greenway\, take all th
 e way to Amboy\nRIGHT on Amboy to cross the bridge\nRIGHT into French Broa
 d River Park\, run the loop at the park\nCross back over the bridge on Amb
 oy and run the Greenway back to the roundabout\nFollow Lyman back to OLR
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/312835128/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260111T194423Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260111T194423Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Avl Digital Nomads": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/314198856/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_314198856@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260418T030449Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T200000
SUMMARY:AVL UX - A First “get to know” the UX community
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nAVL UX (hosted by AVL Digital Nomads) is A
 sheville’s new meetup for UX\, product\, and research folks. This first 
 event is casual and low-pressure and focuses on- quick intros\, small-grou
 p chats\, and a short “what should we do next?” moment.\n\nWhat if Ash
 eville had a regular place where UX people could actually find each other 
 and it without\, feeling like a stiff “networking event”? **AVL UX is 
 Asheville’s new meetup for UX\, product\, and research meant to build an
 d connect the local community to shape what the**\n**UX scene here becomes
 .**\n\nThis first gathering is intentionally **friendly + low-pressure**. 
 Come as you are: working designer\, researcher\, PM\, engineer\, student\,
  career-switcher\, or just UX-curious. The goal is simple: meet people\, t
 rade notes\, and leave with new connections (and a clearer idea of what AV
 L UX should be next).\n\n**What to expect**\n\n* Quick welcomes + name tag
 s (so it’s easy to meet people).\n* Casual small-group conversations and
  prompts (And hopefully no awkward interactions).\n* A short “what shoul
 d AVL UX do next?” moment (talks\, portfolio nights\, design jams\, a Co
 nfig watch party 2026\, etc.)\n\n**A few topics up for discussion**\n\n* *
 *What’s your Asheville UX Scene?:** Where is everyone and what is everyo
 ne doing in Asheville? Why UX here as the industry is rather small\n* **De
 sign-to-code + vibe-coding workflows:** what’s actually working with too
 ls like Figma Make/MCP + Cursor—and what breaks in real teams?\n* **Acce
 ssibility is becoming the baseline:** how are you baking WCAG 2.2 into des
 ign + dev early (instead of last-minute fixes)?\n* **Design systems + toke
 ns in 2026:** how do we keep tokens clean\, scalable\, and synced between 
 design + code without “token rot”?\n* **Calm\, mindful UX:** how do we
  reduce cognitive load and create more “human” experiences instead of 
 noisy\, attention-grabby UI?\n\nFor our first meeting we’ll go to Hi-Wir
 e Brewing in RAD. Easy to get to with plenty of parking. A great assortmen
 t of both alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages. Typically there is a food
  truck as well.\n\nLooking forward to meeting everyone and launching our n
 ew UX community!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/314198856/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260409T155708Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260409T155708Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
