BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/third-thursday-11-5/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T210000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230443
CREATED:20260414T144046Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T204153Z
UID:10005977-1779382800-1779397200@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Third Thursday featuring Jackson Grimm and Clint Roberts of Holler Choir
DESCRIPTION:This month Asheville-based\, nationally recognized musicians Jackson Grimm and Clint Roberts will play in the Museum’s Atrium from 6-8pm. Grimm and Roberts\, who also play in popular band Holler Choir\, bring together old time\, swing band music with indie rock creating a unique and satisfying sound. Sit and listen for a while\, grab a drink from our Perspectives Cafe pop up bar\, and then take some time to stroll the galleries and discover your favorite artworks at night! And don’t forgot to stop by the Studio and silkscreen yourself a poster to take home! \nJackson Grimm is an accomplished and respected band leader\, multi-instrumentalist and teacher in the Western North Carolina music community. His songs marry folk pop melodies with the lonesome sound of traditional Appalachian music. In a region with a strong music culture\, it is no surprise that Grimm’s songwriting is representative of his musical birthplace: Asheville\, NC. \nGrimm won the 2025 LEAF Songwriting competition and has been a 2 year finalist for the Songwriter Serenade. He has shared the stage with and opened up for acts such as Molly Tuttle\, Sierra Ferrell\, Shadowgrass\, the Wilder Flower\, Arlo Guthrie\, Tim Grimm\, Ben Bedford\, Ordinary Elephant\, Nathan Evans Fox\, and more.” \nClint Roberts was raised in the Appalachian mountains of Western North Carolina and crafts songs that bridge the gap between the region’s deep-rooted folk traditions and the contemporary Americana heard on national airwaves. After dedicating a decade to his solo singer-songwriter career beginning in his early twenties\, Clint founded the collective-driven string band Holler Choir in Asheville\, NC\, in 2021. \nSince then\, Holler Choir has toured extensively across the United States and expanded its creative reach by becoming the backing band for a second project\, the Susto String Band\, formed in collaboration with the band Susto. In 2024\, songwriter and multi-instrumentalist Jackson Grimm joined both Holler Choir and the Susto String Band and now co-leads the project alongside Clint.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/third-thursday-11-5/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Performance,Third Thursday
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Grimm-and-Roberts.jpeg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Asheville Art Museum 2 South Pack Square Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2 South Pack Square:geo:-82.5512827,35.5946714
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Runners": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/312835131/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_runners
X-SOURCE:Asheville Runners
UID:event_312835131@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260418T030447Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T200000
SUMMARY:Thursday Run 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Runners\nCome run 1\, 3\, or 6 miles and stay for a 
 beer and soccer tennis after at Olde London Road.\n\nRoutes-\n1 miler:\nRI
 GHT out of OLR parking lot\nContinue around roundabout at Clingman\, and h
 ead toward the river on Lyman St.\nRIGHT on River Arts Place\nCross Rivers
 ide onto the Greenway\nRight on the Greenway to the Craven St Park put in 
 (the dock)\nTurn around and go back the same way to OLR\n\n3 miler:\nStart
  the same as 1 miler\nContinue onto Craven St. Bridge\nLEFT onto Greenway 
 after bridge\nFollow Greenway all the way until it ends at Haywood Rd.\nRI
 GHT onto Haywood Rd\, go across the bridge\nCross the Roundabout at Robert
 s St. and continue onto Clingman\nContinue on Clingman\nLEFT onto Owens Be
 ll Lane\nLEFT onto Hilliard at the top of the hill\nLEFT onto W Haywood\, 
 follow all the way down to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts\nFollow Roberts back
  to OLR\nPass OLR to Bartlett\, turn around and come back to OLR\n\n6 mile
 r:\nAfter the W Haywood downhill to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts St. take to
  Lyman and head back to the Greenway\nLEFT onto the Greenway\, take all th
 e way to Amboy\nRIGHT on Amboy to cross the bridge\nRIGHT into French Broa
 d River Park\, run the loop at the park\nCross back over the bridge on Amb
 oy and run the Greenway back to the roundabout\nFollow Lyman back to OLR
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/312835131/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260111T194429Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260111T194429Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
