SUMMARY:May 23rd Community Cuddles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space.[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-U
 S/ticketing/may-23rd-community-cuddles)**[Click HERE to register!](https:/
 /www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/may-23rd-community-cuddles)**\n\n**This is 
 a non-sexual touch based event that invites participants to explore platon
 ic intimacy in a safe environment** with like-minded people. We respect pe
 rsonal boundaries and through a supportive framework of mutual agreements 
 that maximize safety and create a space of easy openness and compassionate
  connection.\nAt this event we have the chance to normalize touch with cle
 ar boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, consent-based touch. We a
 llow ourselves to be seen. We have fun.\nWe welcome people of all backgrou
 nds\, genders\, ethnicities\, relationship styles\, sexualities\, sizes\, 
 and ages (18+).\n\n**THE RULES**\n1\\. Clothes stay on for the whole event
 \\.\n2\\. You do not have to touch anyone at this event\\.\n3\\. You must 
 receive a verbal YES before you touch anyone\\.\n4\\. Take care of yoursel
 f and those you choose to interact with\\.\n5\\. Speak up if you have a qu
 estion\\\, concern\\\, or if you need assistance with anything during the 
 event\\.\n6\\. All emotions are welcome\\- we love vulnerability\\.\n**WHY
  CUDDLE?**\nTouch is a basic human need\, and many of us do not get enough
 \; most people don’t even know they are missing touch\, or have a way to
  ask for touch without sexualizing it. We believe deeply in the power of t
 ouch\, and the importance of communication and consent in creating a safe 
 space for touch.\nCUDDLING WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers sounds 
 weird or scary to most people. “Will I like it?” “What if someone wa
 nts to touch me and I don’t want to?” “What if I say yes and it’s 
 not what I want?” “What if I really want to touch someone and they say
  no?” These are all normal questions. The answer is that this is a space
  created to ask for exactly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you don’
 t want. Many people start out nervous at a cuddle event & most are really 
 glad they came.\n\n**Schedule:**\n6:50-7pm: Arrive with snacks to share! G
 et comfortable\, meet\, mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circle- its man
 datory. We will set our container\, talk about personal boundaries\, commu
 nication\, & consent.\n7:15pm: Icebreakers and connective activities.\n8:0
 0pm: Open cuddling! You MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ before touchin
 g or cuddling with anybody at this event. If you are not sure how to do th
 is – great! – we will talk about it during the welcome circle.\n10:50p
 m: Closing Circle\, cleanup and head home.\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n* ARRIVE ON T
 IME: It is important that all participants arrive before the Welcome Circl
 e. The Welcome Circle serves the purpose of creating the safe space for co
 nsensual\, non-sexual touch between participants and making sure that ever
 yone is informed about consent.\n* Please arrive clean & as scent free as 
 possible.\n* BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this even
 t.\n\n**WHAT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to share\, a fri
 end\, a date – whatever cuddle accessories you like! The only thing that
  you are required to bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nThese events are n
 ot "gender balanced".\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!*
 * If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not sa
 fe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing
  our best to create a safe environment which means that if someone is caus
 ing harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includ
 es harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors
  and know that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based 
 trauma.\n\n\\*refund policy-\nFull refund if you cancel 7 days before the 
 event or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to cov
 id/flu.\nCredit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days befo
 re an event.\nNo refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-sho
 w.
