SUMMARY:Holiday Weekend Sunday Walk at Little Champion Plant in Waynesvill
 e
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nWhat better way to spend 
 the Sunday afternoon before Memorial Day than by walking with a meetup gro
 up?\n\nOld Timers call this property on Old Howell Mill Road near Old Ashe
 ville Highway "Little Champion" because the Canton Champion Paper Mill put
  in this plant to put wax on paper for making milk cartons. The Mill chang
 ed hands several times\, but the Old Timers kept calling it Little Champio
 n. (Note that Google Maps calls it Evergreen Packaging\, and the sign on t
 he building now says Suzano.)\n\nThe 3/4-mile walking track at Little Cham
 pion runs by Richland Creek with lots of creekside trees\, by fishing spot
 s\, and by a picnic area. There is a bathroom in the middle of the track. 
 We plan to do 4 clockwise laps. (Yes\, you are free to do fewer or even mo
 re!) That will make a total of 5 KM/3.1 miles.\n\nBe sure you enter the pr
 operty on the Old Asheville Highway (east) side of the plant (the side wit
 h the Suzano sign) on Ken Thompson Drive\, go to the rear of the building\
 , and then turning left\, go ***all the way to the far end of the back of 
 the parking lot\, down by the sign designating the Drop Lot***. It is in t
 hat corner of the parking lot where we will assemble. (If you go down the 
 stairs into the middle of the track\, you will be in the wrong place and w
 ill miss where the group is assembling.)\n\nDress appropriately for the we
 ather\; consider a hat and sunscreen. There is a little hill on each lap\,
  so some may want walking sticks. Bring plenty of water and a protein snac
 k. This is a paved track\, so tennis shoes will be fine. Dogs are welcome.
  Strollers will have no problem.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314137743/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260405T201740Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260405T201740Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
