SUMMARY:May 29th An Evening of Spicy/Sensual Snuggles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space.[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-U
 S/ticketing/may-29th-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles)**[CLICK HERE TO PURCH
 ASE YOU TICKET AND RESERVE YOUR SPACE FOR THIS EVENT.](https://www.zeffy.c
 om/en-US/ticketing/may-29th-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles)**[ ](https://w
 ww.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/may-29th-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles)\n\n*
 *What is a Sensual Snuggle Event?**\nThis is a sweet & welcoming event whe
 re we practice and use verbal consent to connect and share touch. We talk 
 about boundaries and practice both saying and receiving a “no”. In thi
 s space it is common to see people cuddle\, share massage\, have their hai
 r brushed\, kiss\, expose nipples\, play\, laugh\, cry\, and be vulnerable
 . This is a sober space where we can relax and connect with other humans w
 ho are seeking touch based connection.\nWe strive for this to be a safe ev
 ent. Safe touch enhances our ability to connect with and trust people. Whe
 n we are in a space of safety\, we are able to relax\, feel comfort\, and 
 be vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\n1- We ask for what we want an wait 
 for a yes before touching others.\n2- We say no if we don’t want to do s
 omething.\n3- We try to receive a no with grace and not take it personally
 .\n4- We arrive on time\, clean (as scent free as possible)\, and sober.\n
 5- We keep our pants/shorts on at this event. (Tops are optional\; this is
  a sensual space\, not a sexual space.)\n6- We are here to connect with ot
 hers. Connection can be verbal\, platonic\, or spicy!\n7- We welcome diver
 sity. Isms and Phobias are not welcome here!\n\n**Who should attend:**\nPe
 ople who are interested in safely exploring touch and sensuality with stra
 ngers. This includes people who are single\, people who are not single\, c
 ouples\, folks who are new to town and looking for connection\, people of 
 all/any genders and sexual orientations\, people of all ages (18 and up). 
 People who understand and respect consent\, who will take care of themselv
 es and people around them. This event is queer-normative. The guest list w
 ill include all genders\, orientations\, ages\, and personalities. If that
 ’s not your thing… This is not the event for you.\n***Who should NOT a
 ttend:***\n-People who are only looking for a sex party.\n-People who do n
 ot understand and respect consent.\n-People who have extreme fear of setti
 ng and speaking their personal boundaries\; in order to create a safe spac
 e we need to know that you will say “no” if you feel a no.\n-People wh
 o are homophobic\, racist\, sexist\, ageist\, ableist…\n-People under 18
  years of age.\n***Schedule of the Evening***\n\n* 6:50pm Doors Open\, Mix
  & Mingle\n* 7:00pm We gather in a circle to meet each other\, build a con
 tainer\, cover consent and boundary setting and discuss event agreements. 
 Then we will play a few intimacy building games to meet and connect with o
 ther people in the room. Please make sure you arrive on-time!\n* 8:15pm On
 ce the container is built we will have self directed snuggling and sensual
  interactions until the end of the party.\n* 10:50pm Closing Circle\; a ti
 me to re-center and connect as a group to verbally share anything that cam
 e up at the event or to voice gratitude to someone(s) you enjoyed interact
 ing with.\n* 11:00pm cleanup & head home\; you are welcome to help.\n\n**W
 e take individual and group safety seriously!** If you experience\, see\, 
 or know that one of our participants is not safe to be at this event we wa
 nt to know about it. We are committed to doing our best to create a safe e
 nvironment which means that if someone is causing harm (physical or mental
 ) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm that takes place out
 side of our events). We stand behind survivors and know that some of our p
 articipants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\nThese events are 
 not "gender balanced"[. Check out our website for more information about t
 his decision. ](http://holdmeavl.com/why-i-dont-gender-balance-events/)\n\
 n**Simple definitions/clarifications-** Platonic- marked by the absence of
  romance or sex.\nMost of the interactions we have with friends and strang
 ers are platonic.\nSensual- gratification of the senses or the indulgence 
 of appetite.\nWe might feel sensual when we feel someone's breath on our n
 eck or experience a extra long and slow caress.\nSexual- having or involvi
 ng sex.\nOften involving one more more peoples genitals\; perhaps seeking 
 orgasm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full refund if you cancel 7 days before the eve
 nt or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid.
  Credit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before an ev
 ent. No refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
