BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/adult-studio-landscape-wild-and-free/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260530T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260530T160000
DTSTAMP:20260417T230443
CREATED:20260123T211519Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260206T160753Z
UID:10005991-1780146000-1780156800@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Adult Studio: Landscape // Wild and Free
DESCRIPTION:Join instructor Ehren Fritz Gerhard in this three-hour session of plein air painting on location at Zealandia Estate! Students will interpret the landscape using a combination of abstract and realistic painting techniques. Learn how to utilize a limited color palette and limited brushes to emphasize the fundamental structure of your paintings. Minimalism in the landscape\, expressive color palettes\, bold brushstrokes\, and visual contrast will be the primary focus of this session accompanied by instructor demonstration\, guidance\, and group critique. \nEhren Fritz Gerhard completed his Master of Fine Arts from Arizona State University in 2013 and Bachelor of Arts from Florida Gulf Coast University in 2009.  He has been an Adjunct Professor of Drawing and Printmaking at Florida Gulf Coast University as well as Basic Design and Color Theory at Florida Southwestern State College. He lives in Asheville\, North Carolina with his wife\, daughter\, son\, and dog where he maintains an active studio\, works on his garden and goes on primitive camping and fishing trips as often as possible. \nREGISTER HERE \nEhren Fritz Gerhard\, Poppin’ Daisies\, acrylic and pastel on canvas\, 60×60 inches \nEhren Fritz Gerhard\, Bros Under the Sun\, acrylic on canvas\, 10×8 inches \nEhren Fritz Gerhard\, Zinni Yucca\, acrylic on canvas\, 8×10 inches
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/adult-studio-landscape-wild-and-free/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Adult Studio
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Poppin-Daisies-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
